      "side": 1,
      "message": "These tuning sysprops have historically gone poorly. 99% of new devices are setup by copy/pasting from previous, so we used to get hit with all sorts of wonky values.\n\nCan you instead give the `initialMaxSurfaceAreaScale` a try? https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/libs/hwui/MemoryPolicy.h;l\u003d44\n\nWe don\u0027t currently use that in any shipping memory policy, but it has been experimented with in the \"extremelowram\" policy (see MemoryPolicy.cpp). A policy for these devices that configures that would be more palatable than this sysprop, as at least then the intention is understood and there\u0027s a recovery if the device gives a bad value or mis-judges an actual app\u0027s usage",
      "revId": "fde9229bce4ce47ffe1339573b4e6d498f48b1bf",
